values ('e9f0a1b2-3c4d-4f38-9b78-8c9d0e1f2a88', 'literary-theory-and-criticism', 'Literary Theory and Criticism', 'Frame literary theory as disciplined inquiry into how texts mean, how readers interpret, and how institutions define literary value. Topics cover formalism and close reading, structuralism and narratology, reader-response and reception, Marxist criticism, psychoanalysis, feminist and queer theory, critical race and decolonial thought, postcolonial and world literature, new historicism and archives, disability and affect, ecocriticism, digital humanities, research design, and a theory-driven critical project.');

